### Togetherly environment template
# Copy to `.env`, edit values, then load with `dotenv`, `direnv`, or your secret manager.
# Keep real secrets in a vault (1Password, Doppler, Render/Fly secrets, etc.) and rotate quarterly.

## Core application
SECRET_KEY=dev-secret-change-me
FLASK_ENV=development
PORT=5001
ALLOW_DEV_DEBUG=1
ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com
DEV_ADMIN_PW=OHsj1984

## Database
# Local default uses swelly.db (SQLite). Override with DB_PATH for custom locations
# or provide a DATABASE_URL/connection string for managed Postgres in production.
DB_PATH=swelly.db
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/swelly

## Stripe (test values shown)
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_REPLACE_ME
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_REPLACE_ME
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_REPLACE_ME
STRIPE_TEST_PRICE_ID=price_REPLACE_ME
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_REPLACE_ME
STRIPE_SUCCESS_URL=http://localhost:5001/
STRIPE_CANCEL_URL=http://localhost:5001/

## Google Gemini (required for AI features)
# Get your API key from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GENAI_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME_WITH_YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY

## OpenAI (optional — leave blank to use the built-in generator)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-REPLACE_ME
OPENAI_GENERATE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

## GitHub feedback automation (Priority 0)
# Provide a PAT with Issues: Read/Write scope and the repo owner/name.
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_REPO=humble-scott-jones/swelly
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TEMPLATE_GENERAL=user-feedback
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TEMPLATE_THUMBSDOWN=thumbs-down
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TIMEOUT=6.0

## Rate limits & quotas
REELS_QUOTA_MONTHLY=30
TEAM_MEMBER_LIMIT=10

## Hashing + auth (optional overrides)
# FAST_PASSWORD_HASH=12000
# PASSWORD_HASH_METHOD=pbkdf2:sha256:260000

## Misc toggles
# USE_OPENAI_FOR_POSTS=1
# RUN_UI_SMOKE=1

# Notes:
# - This template intentionally includes placeholders for production secrets; do not commit real values.
# - Store the canonical values in your secret manager and export them via `op inject`, Doppler, etc., before deploying or running smoke tests.